WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.634
Ukraine says its defenses

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.303
managed to shoot down 29

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.304
out of 30 missiles

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.438
fired in an overnight

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:06.806
countrywide bombardment.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.041
Here you see one

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.542
of those interceptor missiles

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.243
this is one

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.379
that was targeting the capital of Kiev.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.214
Ukraine's military says one civilian

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.216
was killed by fragments of a missile

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.217
that was shot down

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:19.052
and two other civilians were injured.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:19.719
CNN's Sam

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.821
Kiley is in southeastern Ukraine for us.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:22.555
So, Sam,

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.190
Russia has claimed that it struck

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.859
a Ukrainian arms depot.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.661
Is there any truth to that?

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:31.731
There may be.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.600
We wouldn't be allowed to report it

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.036
if it was we. I front can be honest.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:38.104
We simply don't know.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.073
There have been Russian

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:40.907
air strikes

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.243
that have been successful in attacking

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:45.045
logistics nodes

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:45.845
of the Ukrainian

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.281
armed forces in the past.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.316
But the Ukrainians insist that

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.886
only one of those 30 missiles

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.021
fired at its territory got through.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:57.057
One person was killed in Odessa,

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.492
we believe, by the descent of wreckage.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:02.529
So there is one missile unaccounted for

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:04.464
and we don't know where it went.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:07.133
But this is part of the Ukrainian effort

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.102
to try to make sure that the Russians

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.237
do not manage to adjust their fire

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:12.872
and targeting.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:13.907
Based on the information

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:14.841
they may get from us,

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:18.578
from social network bloggers and others

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.212
more widely.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:19.879
I think, Brianna,

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.748
the really key issue here

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.650
is the relentless

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.618
pace of these air attacks.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.787
We're now seeing them on a scale

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.556
that a few months ago we'd see

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.891
perhaps weekly, perhaps every ten days.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.493
Now we're seeing them

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.994
on a very significant scale

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.229
nearly every night,

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.964
particularly large numbers

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:40.700
of cruise missiles being fired some 30

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:41.701
last night.

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:45.105
Fewer of this short haired, low level

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:45.972
or low,

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:49.542
low tech drones manufactured in Iran,

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.778
but all clearly focused on

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.480
trying to overwhelm, obviously,

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.481
the air defenses here

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.448
and soak up

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.317
the ability of the Ukrainians

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.218
to defend themselves.

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:58.751
I think

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.587
ahead of what the Ukrainians are saying

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:02.288
is a coming summer offensive.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:02.689
In short,

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:03.623
the Russians want to be able

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.358
to safely get into the air

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.694
and support their troops when it comes to

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.431
an increase in the pace and

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.366
violence of the ground war, which,

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.934
of course, is continuing,

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.605
particularly around the city of Bachelet.

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:18.905
All right.

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:19.639
Sam Kiley

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.541
live for us in southeastern Ukraine.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.676
Thank you for the latest in on the war.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.278
We appreciate it, Jim.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.112
For the first time,

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:26.779
we are learning

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:27.447
that Ukraine

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:30.450
has fired the long range storm shadow

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.319
missile successfully at Russian targets.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.721
The UK provided

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.589
the cruise missile ahead of Ukraine's

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.725
highly anticipated counter-offensive.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:39.592
A short time ago,

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:40.827
I spoke with the UK

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:41.761
secretary of State

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.830
for Defense, Ben Wallace.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.166
And here is our conversation beginning

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:46.966
with those missiles

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:50.637
Well, look how

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:50.937
we just

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.172
got informed by the Ukrainians

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.706
that they had successfully used them.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.910
I presume by that it has been successful.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.945
I don't know the full details

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.380
We obviously, like

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.114
the other allies,

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.550
are not involved in such detailed

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.485
use of our gifting.

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:08.354
We we just make sure that they are gifted

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:09.322
what they request

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.191
and we do it within the boundaries

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:12.725
of whether it's obviously in accordance

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:14.194
to helping Ukraine defend itself

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:14.627
and making

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.763
sure that it's a calibrated response.

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.565
All I can confirm is,

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.266
is that it has been used successfully.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.034
That is the information

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.902
I received from the Ukrainians,

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.871
and I'm pleased that it is helping them

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.673
to defend their country.

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:27.540
Looking ahead, this is,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.408
of course, central.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.643
This is one of many weapons systems

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:31.611
considered central

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:32.912
to the highly anticipated

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.148
Ukrainian counteroffensive.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.316
In your view.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:37.217
Does Ukraine

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.952
have all it needs

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:39.419
to order

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:41.221
the start of that offensive when they

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:41.654
are ready?

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:44.090
It definitely has

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.793
a significant part of what it needs to

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.728
to start an offensive

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.196
when the time is just right

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.631
by their military commanders

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.665
and their political leaders.

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.334
And you know that the West,

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.436
the United States, United Kingdom

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.638
and the rest of many of the powers

00:03:58.638 --> 00:03:59.539
in Europe have donated

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:00.840
significant amounts.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.275
We've also a company

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.143
that was training to make sure

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.912
that they are not only basically trained

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.047
but also trained to a more advanced level

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.582
to deliver some combined arms.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:10.149
But, you know,

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:10.617
it's easy

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:10.950
for me

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.352
to say thousands of miles away

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:13.286
and anywhere else,

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.487
you know, everyone should get on with it.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:15.321
It's not going to be me

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.289
that fixing a bayonet

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:18.124
and walking towards a machine gun

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.359
and all the difficult tasks

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.260
that Ukrainian leaders

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.661
are going to have to task.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:22.428
But I think

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.030
I think we are over a year

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:24.897
on, we're in a position

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.199
where the Ukrainians

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:27.433
now have in many areas

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.369
some advantages over the Russians

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:30.837
and should they seek to

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:32.872
to try and push them back.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.172
You know,

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.140
it is clear

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.408
they could be able to do that.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:36.876
But, of course, you know, we'll see.

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:37.944
War is unpredictable.

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:39.012
We when I was serving

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:39.612
in the armed forces,

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:41.648
we used to say no plan survives

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:42.882
contact with the enemy

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:43.983
and we'll see how it goes.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.485
But Storm Shadow

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:46.386
just like the US

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:46.953
drifting hi,

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.121
Miles are very, very important

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.589
components of allowing Ukraine

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.024
to be successful.

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:53.359
If Ukraine chooses to attempt

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:54.360
to take back

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.561
Russian territory

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:56.462
in Crimea,

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:57.330
as well as the eastern

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.965
parts of the country.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.233
Would the UK support that

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.601
if that's their decision to do so?

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.305
It's their sovereign soil.

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:05.638
It's a bit

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:07.573
like you asking me if

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.976
the US were choosing to take back

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:10.810
parts of Texas

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.179
from an enemy that had invaded it.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:13.846
You know,

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:14.347
you wouldn't

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.648
you wouldn't take anyone else from abroad

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:16.949
telling you what you can

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.017
and can't take back.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.053
It is it is Ukrainian soil.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:21.788
It is their sovereign territory.

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:23.389
It's been invaded

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.058
they've lost thousands of lives

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:27.126
as a result of that invasion.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:28.161
And I think ultimately

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.395
it'll be Ukraine's decision

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.430
under international law.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.465
They have every right to do that.

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.600
In accordance of self-defense.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.068
Britain isn't

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:36.803
going to stand in the way of that.

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:37.570
But I think, you know,

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.871
we are a long way from that

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:39.872
where we're in a position

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.940
where at the moment

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.208
the Russians have lost

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:43.409
consider amounts of land

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.211
that they took in February last year,

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.245
but they still hold on

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.814
to significant amounts.

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.682
And it will be for Ukraine to decide

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:50.883
what access,

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.352
what advance they make and

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.053
and where they do it within that country.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:56.022
As you know,

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.257
US officials have publicly warned China

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:00.393
from supplying arms to Russia

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.161
for the war in Ukraine.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.663
Has chided China to date

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:05.298
heeded those warnings.

00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:06.199
Is there any evidence

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.701
that it has supplied lethal military aid?

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:10.570
Well,

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:11.170
I think one of the most

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.672
disappointing things for Russia

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:14.574
throughout this process is that

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:15.742
China has hardly been

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:16.476
a full throated

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:19.479
supporter of Russia we've seen in the UN.

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:21.414
China has consistently abstained

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:22.982
it hasn't voted in favor.

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:23.416
In fact,

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.451
we saw, I think recently a vote

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.186
in another UN body

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:27.754
where effectively

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:29.722
China went against Russia.

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.858
And we haven't seen to date

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:34.527
any more than words and a bit of support

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:35.795
that could change.

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:37.730
And I think that's why the United States

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:38.898
issued that warning.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.199
That could change.

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:42.301
But for now, I think Russia

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.770
Russia has demonstrated to China

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.472
that this war was a bad choice by Russia.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:48.307
I think China recognizes

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:49.776
that it also has a friendship

00:06:49.776 --> 00:06:50.743
with Ukraine

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:51.511
that this is bad

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:52.545
for business, it's bad

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:55.181
for instability, is bad for China.

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:56.182
And therefore,

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:57.250
I don't think it's in China's

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.785
interest to fuel

00:06:58.785 --> 00:07:00.820
a disastrous war with more weapons.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.455
So I think for now,

00:07:02.455 --> 00:07:02.889
the US

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:03.990
and most disappointed by

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.425
China will be Russia.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:06.692
For all of the talk,

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:07.760
Russia's friend

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.362
hasn't come to the rescue.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.363
And secondly,

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:11.998
Ukraine are making advances.

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:12.999
The global community

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:14.367
has a role to play here

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:15.334
in saying to Putin, these

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:16.602
things are unacceptable,

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.137
and that includes China and India.

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:19.439
We did see that publicly.

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:19.906
If you remember

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:20.706
last year,

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:22.475
China and India did say to Putin,

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:23.776
it would be unacceptable.

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:24.877
I haven't seen anything change

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:26.179
from that posture.

00:07:26.179 --> 00:07:27.880
And this is why the Indian community

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.582
is so important in messaging

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:30.416
to President Putin

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:31.884
that his decision was wrong.

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:33.453
He's broken international law.

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:35.154
He should stop his invasion.

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.422
He should reverse it.

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:37.890
And he doesn't have any friends.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.058
I mean, that's the key.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:39.258
You know,

00:07:39.258 --> 00:07:40.827
you don't find China

00:07:40.827 --> 00:07:41.961
a full throated supporter.

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:42.929
You don't find,

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:43.162
you know,

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:45.164
even his Central Asian traditional allies

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:46.699
and are criticizing him for it.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:48.234
He's pretty much on his own.

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:49.469
And I think when everyone else has left

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:51.404
the party, he should reconsider.

00:07:51.404 --> 00:07:52.972
I know the U.K.

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:53.906
and a number of others

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:54.373
have expressed

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:56.442
concern about allies

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:57.877
who might pressure

00:07:57.877 --> 00:07:59.479
Ukraine at some point to

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:01.113
to give up territory

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:02.315
in exchange for a cease fire.

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:04.016
And I personally have heard

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.384
from Western leaders,

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:06.385
particularly in the eastern

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:08.287
part of Europe, concerned

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:10.089
that there are some in Europe

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:12.158
who might apply that pressure to Ukraine.

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:15.061
Are you aware of any such pressure?

00:08:15.061 --> 00:08:18.197
And what would the UK's response be if

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:20.366
if Zelinsky or others were told

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:22.268
hinted in some way?

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:24.971
Listen, you got to make a deal.

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:25.571
When I've worked

00:08:25.571 --> 00:08:26.305
with the Ukrainians on

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:29.075
and off for nearly the last seven years,

00:08:29.075 --> 00:08:31.110
First of all, the Ukrainians are tough

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.212
and pressure will just fall off.

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.113
The main sadness

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:36.082
of any one nation rang out and said,

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:37.917
we think you should do something

00:08:37.917 --> 00:08:39.352
and they don't want to do it.

00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:41.053
They won't be pressurized.

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:42.154
And that's one of the lessons

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:43.155
of the last

00:08:43.155 --> 00:08:44.790
18 months of the invasion

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.225
is that everyone has underestimated

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:47.493
that determination.

00:08:47.493 --> 00:08:49.729
But, you know, I was in Berlin yesterday.

00:08:49.729 --> 00:08:51.163
I saw a very strong resolve

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:52.131
from the German government

00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:53.733
to stand by Ukraine

00:08:53.733 --> 00:08:54.467
to make sure

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:55.735
that they can defend themselves

00:08:55.735 --> 00:08:56.502
and defend

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:57.503
not only the same freedoms

00:08:57.503 --> 00:08:59.171
that you and I enjoy, but also that

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:01.040
they should be allowed to enjoy.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:01.274
You know,

00:09:01.274 --> 00:09:02.308
if you look at the statements

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:03.476
from President Macron

00:09:03.476 --> 00:09:05.077
to President Zelensky's visit,

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:07.813
that's getting tougher towards Russia.

00:09:07.813 --> 00:09:09.715
Not not a watering down

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:10.583
the direction of travel

00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:11.317
of the international community

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:13.219
is actually stronger than it's ever been.

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:15.288
The type of Western systems being gifted

00:09:15.755 --> 00:09:18.491
is another sign of a strong determination

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:20.826
to make sure Russia gets the message that

00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:21.761
we ain't going anywhere.

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:23.229
Understood.

00:09:23.229 --> 00:09:24.330
Well, Mr.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:24.830
Minister, thanks

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:25.631
so much for taking the time.

00:09:25.631 --> 00:09:27.967
We appreciate the conversation

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:29.902
Thank you.

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:30.636
Thank you, Jim.

00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:31.304
Thank you.

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:34.740
The UK is also joining the US in warning

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:36.676
about the rising threat from China

00:09:36.676 --> 00:09:37.710
in Asia. And Boris.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:40.279
I asked the defense minister there

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:42.782
if President Biden's cutting short

00:09:42.782 --> 00:09:45.151
his trip to Asia would send any sort of

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:46.953
signal of weakness to China.

00:09:46.953 --> 00:09:48.354
And he said in his view,

00:09:48.354 --> 00:09:49.922
no, that actions

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:50.423
speak louder

00:09:50.423 --> 00:09:51.958
than words out there, particularly

00:09:51.958 --> 00:09:54.327
the joint US Australian

00:09:54.327 --> 00:09:55.394
UK Defense Treaty.

